  <div class="content-inner"><article class="story"><p class="eyebrow">Organizational update</p><h2>A short pause can be part of moving the mission forward.</h2><p class="lede">This is not a full podcast episode. It is a transparent update from Mikel about why Unmasked Culture became quiet, what changed during that season, and what comes next.</p><p>After a demanding stretch, Mikel made the decision to pause organizational activity for the remainder of the year. An organization centered on mental health could not keep pouring into others while its own team was running on empty, so the pause created room to rest, recalibrate, and return with greater focus.</p><p>During that time, Mikel and his wife became foster parents and learned they were expecting their first child. Alongside a full-time job, youth ministry, web design, and leading a nonprofit, those joyful changes made it clear that his capacity needed honest attention.</p><p>Mikel also reflects on disappointments, including a lightly attended event and releasing work he was not proud of. Rather than allowing those moments to define the organization, he shares renewed confidence in the team, recorded conversations still waiting to be released, and a mission that remains unchanged.</p><blockquote class="quote">Give yourself permission to rest. A pause does not mean the work is over.</blockquote><p>Unmasked Culture remains committed to holistic mental health, vulnerability, and authenticity. The hiatus is ending with fresh energy, a clearer direction, and more conversations ahead.</p></article><aside class="sidebar" aria-label="Update and support links"><h3>Stay connected</h3><p>Explore the full podcast archive, learn more about the mission, or support what comes next.</p><div class="platform-links"><a class="platform-link" href="/podcast"><span><i class="fa-solid fa-microphone" aria-hidden="true"></i>&nbsp; Browse the podcast</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="platform-link" href="/about"><span>